-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 36 ===\nFEDERALREGISTER\nVOLUME 4\n1934 ¿y \n* ^A/ITED ^ NUMBER 67\nWashington, Friday, April 7, 1939\nThe President\nC h il d H ea lth D a y— 1939\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF \nAMERICA\nA PROCLAMATION\nWHEREAS the Congress by joint reso­\nlution of May 18, 1928 (45 Stat. 617), \nhas authorized and requested the Presi­\ndent of the United States to issue an­\nnually a proclamation setting apart May \n1  as Child Health Day; and \nWHEREAS the health of children is of \ngreat concern to all citizens:\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, FRANKLIN D. \nROOSEVELT, President of the United \nStates of America, do hereby designate \nMay 1, 1939, as Child Health Day, and \nurge each community to consider how the \nknowledge of the test methods of pro­\nmoting health may be spread among all \nthose responsible for the care of children \nand how proper provision may be made \nto insure care for the health of all chil­\ndren. And I also call upon the children \nof each community to celebrate this \nyear’s gains in health and growth, and \nto co","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_8078.txt","sha256":"b6a77d98d5469454acd2b586bc9fbe06173d58936fc1aac8f4cc4fb2c1de204a","source":{"line":54,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"41d793dd8a7e1d3a97eaaa0f0e43c4ff9fbaf6d59b7c8d281685cb12b48a38a6"}}]}
